    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a nuanced slate today, with **Gunnar Henderson** (63.69) and **Heliot Ramos** (63.06) serving as our strongest offensive anchors. **Gunnar Henderson** remains a must-start despite facing a lefty in Weathers; his matchup is boosted by an advantageous spot in the two-hole and an 8% lift from his high-efficiency plate appearances. While the slow delivery of the opposing pitcher offers a marginal bump for potential stolen bases\u2014our scarcest and most vital category\u2014the park factors in his venue are the true engine driving his elite status. Similarly, **Heliot Ramos** exploits a highly favorable matchup against Sasaki (xERA 5.30), providing the highest raw skill advantage of the day and allowing us to lean into his mid-order protection.\n\nDeciding between our middle-of-the-order pieces proved difficult, particularly regarding **Josh Jung** (48.40) and **Andy Pages** (43.50). **Josh Jung** actually posted a higher efficiency score than **Andy Pages**, but **Andy Pages** retains his spot due to the structural requirement of maintaining depth across the outfield rotation. Conversely, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (58.38) occupies the UTIL slot; despite a challenging matchup against Rasmussen, his strong xwOBA of .384 and third-spot order anchor make him an essential play over the fringe options currently resting on the bench. We remain cautious of **Kyle Tucker** (53.52) today; while he is a cornerstone of this roster, the 2.60 xERA of McDonald acts as a significant drag on his ceiling, capping his projection despite his favorable batting order position.\n\nWe are actively monitoring the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, whose continued IL stint remains the primary void in our daily output, forcing us to lean heavily on the remaining core. We have successfully avoided the below-floor trap with our starters, ensuring that every bat in the lineup today carries a score above 40.0. With **Jackson Merrill** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** 